  "sectionNotes": "Native towerway exposed foot envelope about23.2x22.2m starts near roof23m, not buried ground foundations. Historic England text gives ground base100ft/30.48m and narrowing to30ft/9.144m below gallery; use this only to extend concealed root columns into building. Native actual above-roof component footprints retain signed positions rather than stretching the whole tower to the article point. Exact facade/roof heights without tags are independent estimates from photos and three-storey description.",
  "sourceFacts": [
    {
      "url": "https://historicengland.org.uk/listing/the-list/list-entry/1205810",
      "usage": "Architectural facts paraphrased from official text only; no supplied photograph/map used.",
      "facts": [
        "Attached quadrilateral brick block has three unequal storeys, north ballroom, central circus and south roof garden.",
        "Four lattice-braced stanchions, each with four constituent pillars, support the open tower.",
        "Main gallery is glass-enclosed; three open galleries and an ogee cap/flagmast complete the crown.",
        "South roof garden has two adjoining pitched glass roofs."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "authoringDirection": "Complete surviving Blackpool Tower open steel lattice, central lift framing, glazed main gallery/three open upper galleries/ogee crown/mast, and intrinsic red-brick three-storey Tower Buildings entertainment block within its exact native outline, including main roofs/clerestories/roof-garden glazing and representative terracotta/arched facade detail. Exclude adjoining independent Art Deco store/clock building and modern shops, neighboring buildings, promenade/beach/pier/seasonal illumination artwork, interior ballroom/circus exhibits, people and copied branding/text. Native tower/component heights and positions control proportions; untagged base roof sections, facade/bay census and concealed details are bounded estimates. Preserve all four open stanchions/diagonal panels/central lift framing rather than solid skillion walls. Use native tower/component sections; retain open space between legs and around lift, open upper galleries and crown. Exact intrinsic block perimeter with north ballroom roof, central raised circus roof/clerestory and two south glazed roof ranges, red-brick/terracotta facade piers/narrow divided white windows/selected half-round upper windows and entry arches. Do not extrude separate Art Deco store/clock building. Architectural members/hidden base and roof subdivisions are medium-fi estimates. No landscape, lighting-artwork, logos, displays, people or interiors.",
